        <p>JUST ONE CASE AS AN INSTANCE.</p>
        <p>The Marvellous Recovery of a Lau</p>
        <p>Lshire Lad Stricken wit!' Paralysis.</p>
        <p>The remarkable experiences of Charles Reynolds, of 92, New Hall-street, Byerden-lane,Burnley, as narrated to a reporter from the " Burnley G.izelte." are as follows ; "Two years ago," said Reynolds, "I was going down the cellar steps, when I caught my foot in some clothes, which sent me spinning on my back ta the battarn. It was a nasty fall, but thinking it might be nothing serious, I took little notice of the pain, and wont on with my work, and played football in all kinds of I weather. I well remember the Thursday I left work. It took mA twenty minutes to get t.) the mill, though it is close by, and half an hour to get back home. A doctor was called in, and then I learned that I had injured my spine. In less than a fortnight the use had gone out of my legs entirely. , the doctor's advice I WW taken to the Burnley HOE- pital in a cab. They put me into bed, and stuck pins into my leas, and the lower parts of the budy, but I Played Football in a couldn't feel anything. Hot and cold water baths and electril batteries were tried, but they made no difference. I wasn't able to deep day or night, and suffered a great deal of misery. Finally, had a chair in which to wheel myself about wit my hands for exorcise, but that did nothing bring any use into my legs. When I had been in th( Hospital three months,and the last examination was cm'</p>
        <p>'</p>
        <p>the nurses said to me, "Poor Cliarles,it's a hal do for pou. What are you going to do row ?" I told them I was going to take one thing which I thought would purl me</p>
        <p>round. They asked what that was, and I told them Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People. I determined to try them. When I got home I persuaded my father to get me a b-,x of Dr. Williams' pink pills. lit first, I took three at a meal, or ninela day. In a fortnight, I begun to move my feet. Up to then they had been absolutely dead. ani I had no feeling in them whatever. In fact, I had ao use in . the body at all below the chest and had to eat . my meals lying down. to! - , , ' When I bad been taking the pills for a month, I could A=-14 1 move my legs altogether, and my back and body seemed to be getting all right. So I got up and cleaned the fire- e 0i ' irons. Then I got a pair of crutches, and begun hobbling about the house with these. Later on I went to the Hos- pital and they were amazed , , to see me. I kept getting .. stronger, and in five or six ' ....4, weeks was able to go - without crutches. They . kinds of weather, asked me how it had come about, so I told them what I had been taking, and that Dr Williams' Pink Pills had done it all. They seemed incredulous, but it is these pills, and these only, that have done it for I have taken nothing else stnce I left the hospital, given up as inclur- able. I have taken about thirty boxes in all, and am taking them still. I can walk without a stick even now, and only take it with me when Igo some distance. I have walked down into Burnley several times, and have been four times te the mill this last week or two, help- ing my father at his looms."</p>
