      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0098" n="art0098">
        <head>EXAMINER, FRIDAY, NOVEMBER 30, 1900.</head>
        <p>THE EXAMINER, FRIDAY, NOVEMBER 30, 1900.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE v. CHESHIRE.</p>
        <p>The members of the Lancashir e County Union met in Manchester on Tuesday evening, and selected the foil )W- -lug to play against Cheshire at Stockport on December Bth. The fifteen is the same th at detested Yorkshire : D Smith (Salford), bauk ; A Field (Rochdale Hornets), R Valentine (Swinton), T WI lliams (Salford), and S Williams (Oldham), three-qua rters ; Arthur Lees (Old- ham), captain, and D Drvies (Swinton). half backs ; G Whitehead (Broughton Range rs), J Rhapp3 and P Tun- ney (Salford),? Treweeke (Bar row), E Vigors (Swinton), W Briers (St. Helens), and J Moffatt and T Fergusson (Oldham), forwards. Reserves : H Proctor (Barrow), back; J Fish (Warringt.,n) and R Messer (Swinton), threequarters; J Lawton (Oldham) and F Morgan (Swin- ton), half backs ; (1 Frater (Otdbarn) and J Roberts Leigh), forwards.</p>
      </div>
