      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0141" n="art0141">
        <p>For the 58 Nearest Estimates of the Number of Tins of Nestle's Milk sold through the Manchester Office during the year ending Wednesday noon, December 12th, 1900. ENTRIES CLOSE AT 12 o'CLOCX (NOON) ON DECEMBER 12TH.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-11-30_WidnesExaminer_art0142" n="art0142">
        <p>INSTRUCTIONS.—Cut off that part of the Label of a lib Tin. of Nestle's Milk across which the . words " Prepared in Switzerland" are printed in red. (This can be easily done by drawing a knife down the Black Lines enclosing this part). On the back of it write your Estimate in Figures, with your Name and Address. Nothing else, please, but write clearly. Post it in an envelope (penny postage) addressed : " NESTLE'S COMPETITION," 63 Corporation St., Manchester.</p>
        <p>N.B.—The Postal Authorities will not carry this for a Halfpenny.</p>
        <p>EMPLOYEES OF THE FIRM MAY NOT COMPETE. IN CASE OF TIES, PRIZES WILL BE DIVIDED.</p>
      </div>
