        <p>----- WARRINGTON CORPORATION. TENDERS ARE INVITED for the ERECTION of the TECHNICAL INSTITUTE, PALMYRA. STREET, WAR- RINGTON. Full particulars can be obtained at the Offices of the Archi- tects. Messrs. William and Segar Owen. Warrington. Builders wishing to tender must send their names to the Architects on or before Saturday. Bth December, 1930, and in due course sets of quantities will be issued to those applying, on deposittof £lO lOs per set, which will be returned on receipt of bona-fide Estimate. ST. AN NEW SCHOOLS.-URGENT APPEAL. The following extracts from Her Majesty's Inspectors of Schools show the great need and extreme urgency for new Schools. "If the increased accommodation for Infants which is much needed in this part of Warrington is not supplied by the extension of these buildings as proposed by the Managers last year, a new school will be required in the immediate neighbourhood." " Her Majesty's Inspector reports that the Class-room of the Junior Mixed Department is habitually used for a larger number of Scholars than that for which it is passed by this Board." " In view of the continued overcrowding of the Senior Mixed Department,and the need for increased Infant ac- commodation the Board of Education trust that they will receive from your Managers, an early intimation, that the plans approved on the 17th April. 1899 will be carried out without delay." SUBSCRIPTIONS may be sent tO.-3t, Anne's New School Fund, Parr's Bank, or to the following Managers :—The Itev J. DAVIES, Chairman, Folly-lane ; EDWARD ROSE, Esq., Treasurer, The Blue Coat School; WILLIAM RICHARDSON, Correspondent. holly Bank, Walton, Warrington ; JOHN BAIRD, Froghall-lane. _</p>
